diagram "The Double Diamond" version=1
theme ink canvas="#FFFFFF" text="#303030" connection="#E91922" radius=0
theme-color design shade=100 fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#E91922" ink="#303030"
subtitle "Discover and Develop expand possibilities; Define and Deliver narrow them."
# v1: structural and appearance refinement; no pins, nudges or manual sizes.
group first "First diamond"
group second "Second diamond"
node discover "Discover" in=first color=design shade=100 shape=diamond
node define "Define" in=first color=design shade=100 shape=diamond
node develop "Develop" in=second color=design shade=100 shape=diamond
node deliver "Deliver" in=second color=design shade=100 shape=diamond
edge e1 discover -> define
edge e2 define -> develop
edge e3 develop -> deliver
layout root row gap=52
layout first row gap=24
layout second row gap=24
note "The reference uses two continuous diamond-shaped regions, not four decision nodes. Native groups cannot draw that boundary."
